  "wallpaper_finding": "The double charge is still present in the replayed arm, and that is expected rather than a failure of the fix. replay_property reuses the stored observed_conditions verbatim (_REVIEW_KEYS) and never re-runs Pass 2d, so a RETRIEVAL-time fix cannot manifest in a replay of a 3.1-era artifact whose conditions were resolved under the old scene set. The exclusion prevents the generic item from being SELECTED in a bathroom on a fresh run; stored artifacts keep the duplicate until they are re-resolved. Tier 2 is where this fix is demonstrated: the item leaves the candidate list of all 33 bathroom rows. The cutover replay from frozen Pass 2c is what clears the stored duplicates.",
  "trim_finding": "The trim op's package effect reproduces the frozen 2026-09-08 measurement exactly (77 identical, 15 support-list-only, 9 shape changes, 1 candidate disappears), which is the instrument check for this run. Unlike the wallpaper op, the trim op is a ROUTE change, which the replay does apply: dispositions are recomputed from the stored verdict against the current route.",
  "wallpaper_package_effect": "None. The both_ops arm produces candidate classes identical to trim_only, so the scene exclusion changes no package candidate on any replayed property.",
